            <div xml:id="d620">

                <pb facs="0598" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.30 Asiatic Fleet/962: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stanton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-29T12:00:00+08:00">November 29,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 2—5:59 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1798. Admiral Glassford and staff left last night aboard the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Luzon</hi> for Manila. The <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Luzon</hi> was accompanied by the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Oahu</hi>. U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Wake</hi> arrived from Hankow
                    yesterday afternoon. Under orders issued by Admiral Hart the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wake</hi> has been partly decommissioned and is to
                    remain in Shanghai to maintain radio communications.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Chungking, Peiping and Manila.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
